{
  "formTitle": "INT-300 Request for Interpreter (Civil)",
  "_comment": "INT-300 comes into the packet when the filer says they need an interpreter in court. The filer completes page 1 and the name line at the top of page 2; the case number is the court's, as on every form in the packet. Item 1 is the filer's own details with their lawyer's information beside them, so it carries the packet's names (person_asking_protection_*, court_name_and_street_address) and is asked once. Item 3's box, 'I need an interpreter in the following language when I am in court', is exactly the answer that switches this form on, so it carries that answer's name (needs_interpreter_yes) and is ticked by it, the way DV-105(A) box 1 carries DV-105's No. Names come from the printed labels and the rectangles, not the XFA paths, which reuse OldHearingTime_dt for three unrelated boxes (item 2's description, item 3's other language, item 4's witness language), ProtectedEmail_ft for the town of origin, and HearingPetitionerRequest_cb for three separate 'Other' boxes. The form has no push buttons.",
